    <item>
      <title>Image Import Refactored</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/image-import-refactored/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 24 Apr 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/image-import-refactored/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Over the course of a few different PRs, developers @wwmayer and @PaddleStroke have re-imagined image import into FreeCAD. Gone is the old &amp;ldquo;Image Workbench&amp;rdquo; &amp;ndash; images are now first-class citizens in FreeCAD, with their import integrated into the core as a normal File-&amp;gt;Open or File-&amp;gt;Import. And this week @PaddleStroke implemented a new (and much more intuitive) user interface for setting the scale of an imported image. This is critical since the most common use of imported images is to match new CAD geometry to the scale in that image.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Radial Gradient Background</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/radial-gradient-background/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Apr 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/radial-gradient-background/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;For many years FreeCAD has supported a linear gradient background: at long last, developer @&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/xtemp09&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;xtemp09&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; has answered the frequent call for a radial gradient. Coupled with @&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/PaddleStroke&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;PaddleStroke&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;rsquo;s rearrangement of the colors Preferences page, FreeCAD now sports an overhauled background option that is sure to make many folks quite happy. Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Easier Unit System Changes</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/easier-unit-system-changes/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Mar 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/easier-unit-system-changes/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;(The new unit system menu in FreeCAD 0.21dev.)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;FreeCAD requires a single unit system to be used throughout the entire program, even if multiple files are open. One of the consequences of that design is that creators who work with multiple unit systems have to switch back and forth between systems regularly. Until now this was quite cumbersome, buried in the Preferences dialog. Thanks to a new menu from developer @&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/PaddleStroke&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;PaddleStroke&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, there is now an alternative. With the merge of &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/8870&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;PR 8870&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, FreeCAD now has an always-available menu for quickly changing the unit system in use.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
