    <item>
      <title>Sketcher Grid Auto-Spacing</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/sketcher-grid-auto-spacing/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 27 Feb 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/sketcher-grid-auto-spacing/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This week saw the merge of a long-awaited Sketcher feature that has been in progress by a team of developers for several months: the Sketcher Workbench now features a massively-refactored grid view that includes automatic-resizing when you zoom in and out, with a refined user interface for turning it on and off and changing the scaling parameters.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Expression Autocomplete Improvements</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/expression-autocomplete-improvements/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 30 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/expression-autocomplete-improvements/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A longstanding bug in FreeCAD was recently tackled by new contributor Adrian Popescu (&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/acpopescu&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;@acpopescu&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;). In &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/8228&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;PR 8228&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and a series of follow-up commits, he has addressed some of the major shortcomings in the expression auto-complete function.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New constraint: Point-on-Spline</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-constraint-point-on-spline/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-constraint-point-on-spline/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In very exciting Sketcher news, Ajinkya Dahale&amp;rsquo;s (@jnxd) work on a the new &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/7782&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;point-on-spline constraint&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was merged late last week and is now available the main development trunk: it will be available in the next weekly development builds as they become available over the next several days.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
