    <item>
      <title>Tangent constraint at B-spline knots</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/tangent-constraint-at-b-spline-knots/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 28 Dec 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/tangent-constraint-at-b-spline-knots/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This past week marked the merge of a feature that&amp;rsquo;s been in development since October: the ability to apply a tangency constraint to a line segment at B-spline knot points. In addition, the B-Spline knots themselves can now be constrained as any other point in Sketcher.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Little Things: Navigation Cube Update</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/the-little-things-navigation-cube-update/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Dec 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/the-little-things-navigation-cube-update/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;One of the elements that nearly everyone who uses FreeCAD has on their screen when working in 3D is the Navigation Cube. It provides a simple way of visualizing your orientation in 3D space, and serves as a simple way to navigate to predefined views (&amp;ldquo;Front&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;Top&amp;rdquo;, &lt;em&gt;et cetera&lt;/em&gt;). A few weeks ago developer &amp;ldquo;adrianinsaval&amp;rdquo; (Adrián Insaurralde Avalos) submitted &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/7876&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;an improvement to the Navigation &lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/7876&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Cube&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; that makes the corners much easier hit-targets, so it&amp;rsquo;s now easier to switch to isometric views of your model without going to the menus. Adrián was assisted in this venture by &amp;ldquo;Rexbas&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;Jolbas&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;donovaly&amp;rdquo; (Uwe Stöhr), so if you appreciate the new, easier-to-use navigation cube, send your thanks their way.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New in 0.20: Improved OpenSCAD compatibility</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-in-0-20-improved-openscad-compatibility/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 14 Dec 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-in-0-20-improved-openscad-compatibility/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;FreeCAD has supported importing *.scad and *.csg files from &lt;a href=&#34;http://openscad.org/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;OpenSCAD &lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;for several years, but supporting the full range of features provided by OpenSCAD is an ongoing project. The FreeCAD 0.20 release brings improved compatibility with several more commands, as well as bug fixes to several existing commands.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Coming Soon: TechDraw ComplexSection</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/coming-soon-techdraw-complexsection/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 09 Nov 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/coming-soon-techdraw-complexsection/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;After &lt;a href=&#34;https://forum.freecadweb.org/viewtopic.php?f=35&amp;amp;t=72026&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;many person-hours of effort&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, last week a new type of section view, &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecadweb.org/TechDraw_ComplexSection&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Complex Section&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, was added to the TechDraw workbench. This new type of section allows essentially arbitrary cross-sections to be extracted from 3D geometry and displayed in TechDraw by specifying a specific object as the &amp;ldquo;profile object&amp;rdquo; to use.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Coming Soon: Sketcher Elements UI Refinement</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/coming-soon-sketcher-elements-ui-refinement/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 02 Nov 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/coming-soon-sketcher-elements-ui-refinement/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;FreeCAD is constantly under development, with people across the world contributing code, documentation, ideas, and more. Recently developer &amp;ldquo;paddle&amp;rdquo; has been working closely with Sketcher lead developer abdullah to refine a &lt;a href=&#34;https://forum.freecadweb.org/viewtopic.php?f=8&amp;amp;t=72239&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;new feature in the Sketcher UI&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and it was merged into the main branch of development this past week. In the new interface, an additional mechanism for selecting and deselecting the points defining geometry elements was created, making it easier to select specific points on a busy sketch.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Addon Spotlight: Assembly Workbenches</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/addon-spotlight-assembly-workbenches/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 19 Oct 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/addon-spotlight-assembly-workbenches/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The current 0.20 release of FreeCAD does not include a built-in workbench for assembling individual components into a more complex system: instead, several 3rd-party addons are available through the Addon Manager, allowing individual users to choose the type of assembly procedure they prefer. Three popular options are A2+, Assembly 3, and Assembly 4. This article will briefly overview each. Note that although the names make it sound like one might be the successor of the other, in fact all three are &amp;ldquo;spiritual successors&amp;rdquo; to the no-longer-maintained Assembly 2 workbench. The order they are presented here (and in the Addon Manager) is alphabetical, not an indication of popularity or &amp;ldquo;official&amp;rdquo; endorsement.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Translating FreeCAD</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/translating-freecad/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Sep 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/translating-freecad/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;FreeCAD is an international project featuring contributors from dozens of countries, and users around the globe. One way we work to improve the usefulness of FreeCAD is by making it available in many different user-interface languages using the crowd-sourced translation platform &lt;a href=&#34;http://crowdin.com/project/freecad&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;CrowdIn&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New in 0.20: Preference Packs</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-in-0-20-preference-packs/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 14 Sep 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-in-0-20-preference-packs/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/releases/tag/0.20&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FreeCAD 0.20&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; features &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecad.org/Release_notes_0.20&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;hundreds of enhancements and bug fixes&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: the new &amp;ldquo;Preference Pack&amp;rdquo; Addon type allows packaging and distribution of any of the settings in a FreeCAD configuration file. The driving application for the new feature was the need to set font and color information along with setting the overall user interface stylesheet, enabling a complete, self-contained &amp;ldquo;theme&amp;rdquo; to be applied in a single button click.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New in 0.20: Sketcher Enhancements</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-in-0-20-sketcher-enhancements/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 07 Sep 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/news/new-in-0-20-sketcher-enhancements/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Of all the &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecad.org/Release_notes_0.20&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;new features&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in the recently-released &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/releases/tag/0.20&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FreeCAD 0.20&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, it&amp;rsquo;s likely that the ones that will affect the most users are the improved tools in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecadweb.org/Sketcher_Workbench&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Sketcher workbench&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
